|retry logic and exponential backoff are not the same|

Retry logic means trying a failed request again.
Exponential backoff means increasing the waiting time between retries.
Example: Banking Bureau API

Remember: Exponential backoff is one strategy used within retry logic. 
Retry logic controls whether to retry; exponential backoff controls how long to wait between retries.

Feature | Retry Logic | Exponential Backoff

Meaning | Tries a failed request again | Retries with increasing wait times

Waiting time | Can be fixed or have no delay | Increases after each failure

Example | 1s -> 1s -> 1s | 1s -> 2s -> 4s -> 8s

Purpose | Recover from temporary failures | Recover while reducing pressure on the API

Banking example | Retry a failed bureau API request after 1 second each time | Retry after 1, 2, and 4 seconds if the bureau API remains unavailable

Limitation | Frequent retries may overload the API | Retries can still fail; set retry limits and timeouts

